  "content": [
    {
      "text": "records of seed of Nephi1 and of Twelve Apostles shall be established in one, 1 Ne. 13:41. there is one God over all earth, 1 Ne. 13:41. the Lord esteemeth all flesh in one, 1 Ne. 17:35. one fold and one shepherd, 1 Ne. 22:25 (3 Ne. 15:17; 16:3; John 10:16). one Messiah spoken of by prophets, 2 Ne. 25:18. the Father, the Son, and the Holy Ghost are one God, 2 Ne. 31:21 (Mosiah 15:2–5; Alma 11:44; 3 Ne. 11:27, 36; Morm. 7:7). one being is as precious in God’s sight as other, Jacob 2:21. Christ and the Father are one, Mosiah 15:4 (3 Ne. 11:27; 19:23, 29; 20:35; 28:10; John 10:30; 17:11, 21–22). Nephites should look forward with one eye, having one faith and one baptism, Mosiah 18:21 (Eph. 4:4–6). ye shall not esteem one flesh above another, Mosiah 23:7. there is only one God, Alma 11:28–29, 35 (14:5; Deut. 6:4; Gal. 3:20; Eph. 4:5–6). Jesus expounds all scriptures in one, 3 Ne. 23:14. Nephites are in one, children of Christ, 4 Ne. 1:17. devil persuades no man to do good, no, not one, Moro. 7:17.",
